# Query LLM Frontend - Cursor Rules

## Project Overview
This is a Next.js 16 React application with TypeScript, TanStack Query (React Query), Firebase Auth, and Tailwind CSS.

## Tech Stack
- Framework: Next.js 16 (App Router)
- Runtime: React 19
- Language: TypeScript
- State Management: Zustand + TanStack Query
- Authentication: Firebase Client SDK
- Styling: Tailwind CSS + shadcn/ui
- Forms: React Hook Form + Zod
- HTTP Client: Axios
- UI Components: Radix UI + Custom Components
- Package Manager: npm

## Naming Conventions

### Files
- React Components: PascalCase - `LoginForm.tsx`, `ChatInput.tsx`, `Sidebar.tsx`
- Pages (App Router): lowercase - `page.tsx`, `layout.tsx`, `loading.tsx`, `error.tsx`
- Hooks: kebab-case with `use-` prefix - `use-auth.ts`, `use-chat-store.ts`, `use-conversation-queries.ts`
- Utils/Libs: kebab-case - `api.ts`, `utils.ts`, `firebase.ts`, `tanstack-query.ts`
- Types: kebab-case - `index.ts`, `tanstack-query.ts`

### Code
- Variables: camelCase - `userData`, `isValid`, `authToken`
- Functions: camelCase - `getUserById()`, `createUser()`, `validateInput()`
- Constants: SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE - `MAX_PAGE_SIZE`, `DEFAULT_LIMIT`
- Types/Interfaces: PascalCase with `T` prefix - `TUser`, `TConversation`, `TApiResponse`
- Type Props: PascalCase - `LoginFormProps`, `SidebarProps`
- Route Groups: (parentheses) - `(auth)`, `(private)`

